# Performance budget (PetCalc)

Enforced by `scripts/audit/budgets.mjs` and `npm run lhci` (`lighthouserc.cjs`). Philosophy: plain HTML, light client JS (`docs/SEO-PLAYBOOK.md` section 2).

## Gzip size limits (defaults)

| Metric | Limit |
|--------|-------|
| First-party JS per page | 25 KB |
| First-party JS per embed page | 15 KB |
| Any single emitted `.js` file | 20 KB |
| Total JS in `dist/` | 200 KB |
| HTML document (incl. inlined CSS) | 60 KB |
| CSS (inline + linked) per page | 25 KB |
| Single image (raw) | 150 KB |

Override via env vars (`BUDGET_PAGE_JS_KB`, etc.) only with measured need documented in PR.

## Lighthouse CI (mobile lab)

- Performance score ≥ 0.95 (median)
- LCP ≤ 2.5s, CLS ≤ 0.1, TBT ≤ 200ms
- Run after enabling `ga4MeasurementId` or AdSense — third-party scripts affect real users even when excluded from budget math.

## Implementation rules

- Put calculator maths in `src/lib/formulas/*`; keep `.astro` scripts thin.
- No new npm dependencies unless bundle impact is measured with `npm run audit:budgets`.
- Reserve dimensions for images and ad slots to prevent CLS.
- Embeds must stay under embed JS budget — no duplicate full-page scripts.

## Pre-merge

```bash
npm run build && npm run audit:budgets && npm run lhci
```

Add new URLs to `lighthouserc.cjs` only when introducing a **new template**, not each tool clone.
